<title>USA: Clinton to propose $100 mln Internet project.</title>
<headline>Clinton to propose $100 mln Internet project.</headline>
<dateline>KNOXVILLE, Tenn. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said Thursday that President Clinton would propose a $100 million project to upgrade the Internet.</p>
<p>Spokesman Mike McCurry told reporters on a flight from Washington to Knoxville that the project is proposed for fiscal year 1998 and would span five years.</p>
<p>He said the objective is to develop a partnership between the public and private sectors to promote more Internet connections with libraries and classrooms, and to increase the overall speed of the Internet.</p>
</text>
